# Milestone: v0.10.12-cat-e-activation
# Covers: D-slotchange-3 determinism rule (spec #4 §7): a sync slot-change
#         handler that triggers a nested slot-change write degrades to async
#         (deferred ring); the deferred entry is dispatched at the next
#         safepoint before urbi_vm_watcher_eval_dirty, producing deterministic output.
#
# blocked: no multi-preset runner mode.  The prerequisites this header
#          used to list -- top-level `var`, Object.new(), `at sync`, and
#          slot-change subscription -- all work now.  What is missing is
#          the repetition and preset sweep the determinism claim needs.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: reactive-slot-change
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture requires:
#     - var declaration at top level (globals exposure, T69)
#     - Object.new() constructor (globals + stdlib, T70+)
#     - at sync (obj.x.changed?) watcher (globals for `obj`)
#     - at (obj.y.changed?) watcher
#     - obj.x = N assignment (globals for `obj`)
#   All require the T69 globals-exposure task.  The underlying deferred-ring
#   drain and reentrancy degrade were tested in unit/test_slot_change_reentrancy.c
#   until the Phase 0 runtime-internals test cleanup; no C-level coverage today.
#
# Activate at T69 by replacing the source below with the uncommented version.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T69):
#   var o = Object.new();
#   var log = "";
#   at sync (o.x.changed?) function (v) { o.y = v + 100 };
#   at (o.y.changed?) function (v) { log = log + "Y" + v };
#   o.x = 1;
#   echo(log);
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "Y101"
